<title>SOUTH AFRICA: GOLF-SOUTH AFRICAN PGA CHAMPIONSHIP LEADING SCORES.</title>
<headline>GOLF-SOUTH AFRICAN PGA CHAMPIONSHIP LEADING SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scores from the</p>
<p>fourth and final round of the South African PGA Championship on</p>
<p>Sunday (South African unless stated):</p>
<p>269 Nick Price (Zimbabwe) 67 66 70 66, David Frost 69 63</p>
<p>66 71 (Price won on first play-off hole)</p>
<p>270 Nico van Rensburg 68 68 66 68</p>
<p>272 Retief Goosen 65 66 70 71</p>
<p>273 Wayne Westner 68 66 71 68, Greg Petersen (U.S.) 71</p>
<p>69 65 68, Marco Gortana 70 67 67 69</p>
<p>274 Matthew Goggin (Australia) 69 69 69 67, Max Anglert</p>
<p>(Sweden) 68 67 69 70, Niclas Fasth (Sweden) 66 69 68</p>
<p>71, Katsuyoshi Tomori (Japan) 67 67 67 73</p>
<p>275 Greg Chalmers (Australia) 70 68 71 66, Sven Struver</p>
<p>(Germany) 71 69 65 70, Craig Kamps 68 68 68 71</p>
<p>276 Trevor Dodds (Namibia) 68 72 68 68, Ignacio Garrido</p>
<p>(Spain) 69 69 67 71, Tony Johnstone (Zimbabwe) 70 69</p>
<p>67 70, Desvondes Botes 68 72 67 69, Bob May (U.S.)</p>
<p>66 68 72 70</p>
<p>277 Michael Archer (Britain) 68 68 74 67, Paul McGinley</p>
<p>(Britain) 71 67 71 68, Gordon Sherry (Scotland) 69</p>
<p>68 71 69, Van Phillips (Britain) 70 64 74 69, Carl</p>
<p>Watts (Britain) 69 69 69 70, Fulton Allem 69 69 69</p>
<p>70, Mark McNulty (Zimbabwe) 69 69 67 72.</p>
